3. Nc3
{ The most popular way for white to continue. Knight to c3 puts more pressure on the center and provides support on the e4 square in case white is able to play e4 right away. }
3... Nf6
{ Black plays knight f6 to put more control on e4, preventing white from playing e4 right away. The knight also puts more defense on d5. }
4. Bg5
{ To get into the Tarrasch, white plays bishop to g5. This is the most common move in this position, pinning the knight to the queen and removing some defense from d5. Capturing in the center will now force black to recapture with a pawn. }
